---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy — TPM">
  <section style="padding: 3rem 0;">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: 2026-04-18.</strong></p>
    <p>TPM runs on your machine. What you see here is how we treat data that flows through our systems.</p>
    <h2>Data we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Device metadata</strong> — a UUID generated on first run, a hashed fingerprint of hostname + platform + CPU. Used for license + anti-abuse.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage logs</strong> — per inference call: timestamp, model, token counts, neurons, session id. Used for quota and billing.</li>
      <li><strong>Audit metadata</strong> (Pro/Team) — audit id, target URL, duration, cost. Synced to your account.</li>
      <li><strong>Audit artifacts</strong> (Pro/Team, opt-in) — YAML / JSON / HTML / PDF outputs synced to R2 for cross-device access.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What we DON'T collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your source code.</li>
      <li>Prompt contents, unless you explicitly enable debug mode.</li>
      <li>The targets you audit (for Free tier).</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — compute (Workers), storage (D1, KV, R2), model inference (Workers AI).</li>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payments. We send them your email and a device id.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
